# CodFlow dashboard (Astro) — local development secrets
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in your values.
# (.dev.vars is gitignored — your real values never get committed.)

# ── Required for local dev ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Better Auth signing secret: the dashboard's alone (cod-server checks its
# tokens against the public keys at /api/auth/jwks). Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# HMAC key shared with cod-server for MCP OAuth login tickets (must be >= 32
# bytes). Set the SAME value on cod-server. Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# MCP_LOGIN_TICKET_SECRET=

# In production both values are set with `wrangler secret put`, never in code.

# ── Build-time client value (not a secret) ────────────────────────────────────

# The cod-server origin the browser bundle calls. It lives here rather than in
# .env because the Cloudflare adapter pushes .dev.vars into process.env, and
# Astro reads env with an empty prefix — so this outranks .env and even an
# inline variable. Production takes its value from wrangler.toml [vars], and
# `npm run deploy` parks this file for the build so it cannot leak into it.
# PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8787
